@@ -3,3 +3,16 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer (RFC 6901)
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns the value of a parsed JSON
+document that a JSON Pointer refers to, e.g. `resolvePointer({ a: [1, 2] }, "/a/1")` is `2`. The empty
+pointer refers to the whole document.
+
+It throws a `SyntaxError` (a `TypeError` for a non-string) when the pointer is not valid, and a
+`RangeError` when it does not resolve: missing member, out-of-range or non-canonical array index, the
+`-` token (which names no existing element), or a step into a primitive. Only own members of objects
+are considered, so `/constructor` or `/length` never reach inherited properties.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test`.
diff --git a/src/index.ts b/src/index.ts
